  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In a January 12, 2026 official statement, Casey Sacks said AI is already reshaping how people live, work, and learn, while education’s path forward is not linear. Sacks said leaders should first engage with AI, receive training, and clarify how AI will augment rather than replace human educators. Sacks also called for guardrails and clear boundaries so AI use does not weaken critical thinking, reasoning, and creativity, and is paired with intentional skill development. Sacks framed the question as whether fear will hold education back or whether imagination will be used to reinvent learning.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s3",
    "s4"
   ],
